<h1 class="h3 mb-3">About Meal Finder</h1>
<p>
  A Rails app for browsing and searching recipes. All data comes from the free
  <a href="https://www.themealdb.com/api.php">TheMealDB API</a> and is copied into the local
  database by <code>db/seeds.rb</code>.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Data sources</h2>
<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Endpoint</th><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Stored in</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>categories.php</code></td><td>Categories with description and picture</td><td>categories</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>list.php?a=list</code></td><td>Areas (cuisines)</td><td>areas</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>list.php?i=list</code></td><td>Ingredients with descriptions</td><td>ingredients</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>search.php?f=a to z</code></td><td>All meals, with up to 20 ingredients and tags</td><td>meals, meal_ingredients, tags, meal_tags</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">How the data fits together</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A category has many meals; an area has many meals (one-to-many).</li>
  <li>Meals and ingredients are many-to-many through <code>meal_ingredients</code>, which also stores the measure.</li>
  <li>Meals and tags are many-to-many through <code>meal_tags</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">ERD</h2>
   <%= image_tag "/erd.png", class: "img-fluid border rounded", alt: "Entity relationship diagram of the database" %>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Rows in the database</h2>
<ul class="list-unstyled">
  <% { "Categories" => Category.count, "Areas" => Area.count, "Ingredients" => Ingredient.count,
       "Tags" => Tag.count, "Meals" => Meal.count }.each do |label, n| %>
    <li><%= label %>: <strong><%= n %></strong></li>
  <% end %>
</ul>
